{"title":"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems\">2020 AMC 10B #16</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Problems\">2020 AMC 12B #14</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Game_Theory)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Game Theory)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Educated_Guess)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Simulation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Simulation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyOfMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bela and Jenn play the following game on the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a585433224883cbcd304f34129a152b97d5ed96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, n]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> of the real number line, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a fixed integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. They take turns playing, with Bela going first. At his first turn, Bela chooses any real number in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a585433224883cbcd304f34129a152b97d5ed96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, n]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />. Thereafter, the player whose turn it is chooses a real number that is more than one unit away from all numbers previously chosen by either player. A player unable to choose such a number loses. Using optimal strategy, which player will win the game?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/993d06d29a2a43795bef43133ef259fddd4db74d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win.} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\text{ Jenn will always win.} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\text{ Bela will win if and only if }n \\text{ is odd.} \\\\ \\textbf{(D)} \\text{ Jenn will win if and only if }n \\text{ is odd.} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\text { Jenn will win if and only if } n&gt;8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Game_Theory.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Game_Theory)\">Solution 1 (Game Theory)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Game Theory)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use game theory.\n</p><p>Notice how they say Optimal Strategy. This means that each player plays the best move in any scene.\n</p><p>We then solve through cases.\n</p><p>We set \\( n &gt; 4 \\), \\( n \\) is even. Say \\( n = 10 \\). Then, we see that Bela could pick either 3 or 4, and then Jenn would be forced to choose either 1(2), 5, or 6. But notice how you can only make one move, and 1 and \\( [5,6] \\) are on opposite sides. So therefore, Bela will always win.\n</p><p>We set \\( n &gt; 4 \\), \\( n \\) is odd. Say \\( n = 9 \\). This is even easier! Bela could just choose the middle, and then again, Jenn would be forced to pick a move that Bela could just replicate and win. So, Bela will also always win.\n</p><p>Through deduction, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934859920053cb934d19b8f99d874f48d2fb6a25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4caa0fcaf0f0488dcf71b3d94f8bbe1a1a0b6c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{But that&#39;s just a theory, a game theory!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"289\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Symmetry)\">Solution 2 (Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Bela selects the middle number in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a585433224883cbcd304f34129a152b97d5ed96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, n]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> and then mirror whatever number Jenn selects, then if Jenn can select a number within the range, so can Bela. Jenn will always be the first person to run out of a number to choose, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934859920053cb934d19b8f99d874f48d2fb6a25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Educated_Guess.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Educated_Guess)\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Educated Guess)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First of all, realize that the parity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> likely has no effect on the strategy, since Bela obviously wins when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and it's not hard to find a winning strategy for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> (start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c8332f3acf37eb5aeaeca80118fd58e33bd93d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />).  Similarly, there is no reason the strategy would change when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b539522a64dacbb7c6e1d01afadaf7e840111b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>So we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c87a7b3c933444ead3bb801ace82823c7282c28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> From here it is best to try out random numbers and try to find the strategy that will let Bela win, but if you can't find it, realize that it is more likely the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66ff56440e542cb2592bbf969696f0ec95a41170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"194\" height=\"28\" /> since Bela has the first move and thus has more control.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Simulation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Simulation)\">Solution 4 (Simulation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Simulation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just play the game. We can draw a number line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and assume Bela and Jenn will only play the integer values. From now after playing one round of the game, Bela will win so answers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/3/db3d47a1e5ac7ba055b88723e7e6c7db2e72bb24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},\\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> are eliminated. Now we want to test if Bela will win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even so we can draw another number line this time up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now after playing the game, we can find that Bela won yet again so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01ce659753bc4be1bb10752c76589b4b6e7e241d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"201\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-minor edits by jjbros\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 5 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Play out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. In the first case, Bela can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and win, and in the second case, Bela can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and win (try it out). This rules out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Next, consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />. Assume for the sake of contradiction that this is true; an alternate way of stating this is that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c107687c2fa648bc55e3ec49a0e770b408db9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, the second player always wins (we ignore the \"only if\" statement). Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18fb781bb0840e30c7a894eac0d3a0f67fcd3157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a win for the second player. Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093e72c1ebd91ade8c33ce3bcc3ccd3e640cad8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. If Bela chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the game becomes an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18fb781bb0840e30c7a894eac0d3a0f67fcd3157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> case where the first player is instead Jenn. However, by the claim that the second player should win <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c107687c2fa648bc55e3ec49a0e770b408db9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, this game should be a win for Bela, but we have already stated that any games with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c107687c2fa648bc55e3ec49a0e770b408db9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> should be a win for Jenn, which is a contradiction. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is incorrect, and so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66ff56440e542cb2592bbf969696f0ec95a41170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ Bela will always win}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"194\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bela can choose the exact midpoint of the number line. Whatever Jenn does, Bela can copy her moves in the opposite side half of the number line. Jenn will always run out of space first.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We test whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is prime, even, or odd, and we find a winning strategy for Bela each time. We can generalize and find that with an optimal strategy, Bela will always win.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0mlJhyy1m4M\">https://youtu.be/0mlJhyy1m4M</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyOfMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3BvJeZU3T-M\">https://youtu.be/3BvJeZU3T-M</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0xgTR3UEqbQ\">https://youtu.be/0xgTR3UEqbQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95